 "annotations": [
  {
   "id": "n-w-home",
   "x": 0,
   "y": -250,
   "w": 820,
   "page": "page-w-home",
   "text": "Home and its states, each at both widths on one row. The width holds the workings: the figure and its pace card left, the reason \u2014 where the money is, then every category worst-first \u2014 right, and reading one against the other is exactly what 360 cannot do. <b>The gauge lives at 360 only</b>, because <i>can I spend this, right now?</i> is asked in a shop with a phone in your hand; at a desk the question is whether you are on pace, and a dial has no memory of yesterday. Each state is its own row because each has its own fix."
  },
  {
   "id": "n-plan",
   "x": 0,
   "y": -250,
   "w": 820,
   "page": "page-plan",
   "text": "Where each naira gets its job, and the only screen whose <i>hero</i> is a figure nobody wants to be large: <b>unallocated</b>. It takes the top slot because it is the number that decides whether the plan is finished, and it is meant to reach \u20a60.00 and disappear. Protection and rollover are their own columns at 1440 rather than marks on a row \u2014 both are decisions about a category, not decorations of it. The 360 row menu is the same two decisions on a screen with no room for columns."
  },
  {
   "id": "n-tx",
   "x": 0,
   "y": -250,
   "w": 820,
   "page": "page-tx",
   "text": "The list, and the two ways of having nothing in it. <b>A standing filter rail at 1440, tabs at 360</b>: stacked filters scroll the list away, and losing your place is the one thing that matters on this screen. <b>Both empty states are their own row</b> because they want opposite things \u2014 <i>nothing recorded</i> wants a movement, <i>filters match nothing</i> wants the filters cleared, and a single \u201cno results\u201d covering both is how a person clears their data looking for a button. Opening balances and debts are dated 24 September, the day before the cycle, so they never count as this cycle\u2019s saving."
  },
  {
   "id": "n-qa",
   "x": 0,
   "y": -250,
   "w": 820,
   "page": "page-qa",
   "text": "The persistent action, and <b>the reason the centre of the bottom bar is not a route</b>: story G2 wants a spend recorded while standing at a counter, so it is the largest target on the screen and it sits under the thumb. At 1440 it is a button in the header and a dialog, because a sheet sliding up a laptop is a phone gesture wearing a suit. <b>Delete is a quiet button, never a red one</b> \u2014 the same rule the primitives sheet sets, and the same one the category row follows."
  },
  {
   "id": "n-dg",
   "x": 0,
   "y": -250,
   "w": 820,
   "page": "page-dg",
   "text": "Both directions of money that is not this cycle\u2019s: what you are saving for, and what is owed either way. <b>Debts loses its tabs entirely at 1440</b>, because the best thing width buys is sometimes one less control \u2014 the two lists sit side by side instead. At 360 they are tabs, and <i>Goals</i> is its own row here for that reason. <b>B. Colleague goes the other way</b>, and the direction is carried by the words <i>owes you</i> rather than by a sign or a colour. The printed record is on Foundations, not here: it leaves the app."
  },
  {
   "id": "n-mo",
   "x": 0,
   "y": -250,
   "w": 820,
   "page": "page-mo",
   "text": "Completed cycles, and the empty state that matters more than the populated one \u2014 a person meets this screen in month one, when there is nothing in it, and it has to say so without sounding broken. <b>A cycle is a salary month, 25th to 24th</b>, not a calendar month, which is the whole reason this screen exists under its own name rather than as \u201cHistory\u201d."
  },
  {
   "id": "n-zk",
   "x": 0,
   "y": -250,
   "w": 820,
   "page": "page-zk",
   "text": "The estimate and its workings, and <b>the workings are the point</b>: zakat is an obligation a person answers for, so every figure that goes into it is shown and named, and the nisab it is measured against is dated. <b>Nothing here advises.</b> The app reports what it can see and says plainly what it cannot \u2014 assets it does not hold, and the year it cannot witness. Sadaqah is a category of its own and is never counted as zakat."
  },
  {
   "id": "n-bank",
   "x": 0,
   "y": -250,
   "w": 820,
   "page": "page-bank",
   "text": "Detected movements, sorted one at a time. <b>Never a list of forms</b>: each one is a decision about real money and a grid of dropdowns is how a person agrees to twelve things they did not read. The duplicate case is the one that earns the screen \u2014 someone who already typed it in by hand should not end up counting it twice \u2014 and <i>nothing to sort</i> is a finished state, not an empty one."
  }
 ],
 "launch": {
  "view": "canvas",
  "page": "page-w-home"
 }
}